== a_loop_variable_that_is_a_variable_too
error[Z0106]: `dose` is both a loop variable or parameter and a variable of d
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:67
  |
2 | for dose in [1, 2] { print(d.plot(x: change, y: change).vline(at: dose)) }
  |                                                                   ^^^^ which one is meant?
  |
  = help: rename the loop variable, or the column with `rename`; inside a frame method a loop variable wins over a column, so a clash is never resolved silently

