== a_bound_number_that_is_no_size
error[Z0401]: `size:` of `points` is the diameter of every mark in points of 1/72 inch, above 0, but this is -2
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:41
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).points(size: big)
  |                                         ^^^ not a size
  |
  = help: write a size such as 3 or 6, or the name of a variable to size the marks by; without `size:` a point takes the size the plot gives, or is 4.5 across
